\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Renderer evidence from Windows headless Chrome, median of three samples per tier with the observed range in brackets; the P95 columns are likewise the median of the three per-sample P95 readings. Hardware rows use the host's integrated Intel GPU through ANGLE; software rows force SwiftShader. On ordinary integrated graphics the render submission work meets the 4.17 ms budget a 240 Hz display would require in all six samples; under software rasterisation all six miss it, and that floor is what the adaptive quality governor exists for. Neither row is a claim about displayed FPS, which the display and browser cap.}}{30}{table.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:renderer}{{6.2}{30}{Renderer evidence from Windows headless Chrome, median of three samples per tier with the observed range in brackets; the P95 columns are likewise the median of the three per-sample P95 readings. Hardware rows use the host's integrated Intel GPU through ANGLE; software rows force SwiftShader. On ordinary integrated graphics the render submission work meets the 4.17 ms budget a 240 Hz display would require in all six samples; under software rasterisation all six miss it, and that floor is what the adaptive quality governor exists for. Neither row is a claim about displayed FPS, which the display and browser cap}{table.caption.13}{}}
