\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces Persona review trajectory across rounds. \textbf  {Every persona in this table is a language-model construct scored by the author, not a person, and no row is user evidence.} The figures are reported as measured by the analyst-run method, with the threats to validity stated below. This was a formative method run before the evaluation harnesses were committed: the per-persona responses behind these means were not retained as a machine-readable artefact, so unlike every other table in this chapter these rows cannot be re-derived from the repository and should be read as a trend record rather than as reproducible data.}}{31}{table.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:persona}{{6.3}{31}{Persona review trajectory across rounds. \textbf {Every persona in this table is a language-model construct scored by the author, not a person, and no row is user evidence.} The figures are reported as measured by the analyst-run method, with the threats to validity stated below. This was a formative method run before the evaluation harnesses were committed: the per-persona responses behind these means were not retained as a machine-readable artefact, so unlike every other table in this chapter these rows cannot be re-derived from the repository and should be read as a trend record rather than as reproducible data}{table.caption.14}{}}
